title: If involved in a collision
pid: bcaae480-35a7-4cdc-9485-fab6b6bafcbe
body: |2-
  - Stop. Check for injuries.
    - If so, call 911 for injuries.
    - If not, move vehicle out of traffic, then call 911.
  - Show your docs to other driver, law enforcement, anyone else involved
    - driver’s license
    - vehicle registration card
    - insurance information
    - current address
  - Report to law enforcement within 24 hours if any injury or death
  - If the other car was empty
    - Try to find the owner.
    - If can't, leave a note: name, phone number, address.
    - Report to law enforcement.
  - If killed or injured an animal:
    - Call the nearest humane society or law enforcement.
    - Don't try to move it.
  - Must report it to DMV within 10 days,
    - if either of
      - The collision caused more than $1,000 in damage to property.
      - Anyone was injured or killed.
    - Applies even
      - for minor injuries
      - on private property
